# Printing numbers from 0 to 3 using a for loop.
# The for loop is a control flow statement that allows you to iterate over a sequence of values, such as a list, tuple, string, or a range of numbers. In this example, we will use the range() function to generate a sequence of numbers from 0 to 3 and print each number in the sequence.
# The range() function takes a single argument, which specifies the end of the sequence (exclusive). In this case, range(4) generates the numbers 0, 1, 2, and 3. The for loop will iterate over each of these numbers, assigning the current number to the variable i in each iteration, and then executing the block of code inside the loop (in this case, printing the value of i).
#The range() function is a built-in function in Python that generates a sequence of numbers. It can take one, two, or three arguments:
# range(stop): Generates numbers from 0 up to, but not including, stop. 
# range(start, stop): Generates numbers from start up to, but not including, stop.
# range(start, stop, step): Generates numbers from start up to, but not including, stop, incrementing by step.  
# In this example, we are using range(4), which generates the numbers 0, 1, 2, and 3. The for loop will iterate over these numbers, and in each iteration, it will print the current value of i. When i reaches 4, the loop will stop executing, and no further values will be printed.

for i in range(4):# This line starts a for loop that will iterate over a sequence of numbers generated by the range() function. The range(4) function generates a sequence of numbers starting from 0 up to, but not including, 4. Therefore, the loop will run for the values 0, 1, 2, and 3. Each time the loop runs, the variable i will take on the next value in the sequence generated by range(4).
    print(i) # This line prints the current value of i to the console. Each time the loop runs, it will output the current value of i, which starts at 0 and increments with each iteration until it reaches 3. When i reaches 4, the loop will stop executing, and no further values will be printed.